      "revision": 1343197013,
      "text": "Erythrina vespertilio is a tree native to north and north-east Australia. Its common names are grey corkwood, bat's wing coral tree, yulbah and the more ambiguous \"bean tree\". In the Western Desert language it is known as ininti and in Arrernte and Anmatyerr it is known as atywerety."
    }
